---
// /join/: how to take part. The Practice Room first, then the private routes,
// then the public ones. People, promises and the call line come from
// site/src/data/room.mjs, so nothing here changes when a date or name does.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import RoomRule from '../components/RoomRule.astro';
import NextCall from '../components/NextCall.astro';
import RoomStatus from '../components/RoomStatus.astro';
import { community } from '../lib/community.mjs';
import { room, rhythm, circle, consented, inboxLine, settingUp } from '../data/room.mjs';
const c = community();
const contact = room.contact;
const mail = (subject) => `mailto:${contact}?subject=${encodeURIComponent(subject)}`;
const coOrganizers = consented(circle.coOrganizers);
const kinds = [
  ['Fix an error', 'A typo, a broken link, a wrong number, a misquoted source.', 'Suggest an edit on the page, or open a “Fix an error” issue.', 'Minutes'],
  ['Add or improve a term', 'A word planners use differently, or one that’s missing.', 'Open a “Terms” discussion with a one-sentence definition.', 'Minutes'],
  ['Work an open problem', 'One of the questions on the agenda, marked good-first or not.', 'Pick one on the <a href="/agenda/">agenda</a> and reply in its thread.', 'An hour or two'],
  ['Propose a change', 'To an idea, a method, or how a section is built.', 'Open a “Proposals” discussion.', 'A short write-up'],
  ['Share a case', 'What happened, with names and numbers changed.', 'Read <a href="/sharing-safely/">Sharing safely</a>, then open a “Cases” discussion.', 'A few paragraphs'],
  ['Add a public source', 'A paper, a talk, a public dataset, a filing.', 'Open an “Add a public source” issue.', 'Minutes'],
  ['Take a role', 'Greeter, call host, channel host, pre-check reviewer and more.', 'Read the <a href="/roles/">role cards</a> and raise your hand privately.', 'A few hours a month'],
  ['Translate a section', 'Into a language you plan in.', 'Open a discussion first, so two people don’t translate the same page.', 'Hours'],
];
---
<Base title="Join in" description="How to take part in the Capacity Planning Practice: join the Practice Room, write in privately, comment on a page, or take a role." nav="join">
  <div class="wrap wrap--reading">
    <div class="page-head reading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Join in</p>
      <h1>Work the open problems with other planners. Start with one comment, or one email.</h1>
      <p class="lede">You can take part in public, on GitHub, or in private, through the Practice Room and the mailbox. A good correction counts as much as a new section.</p>
    </div>

    <section class="prose reading" aria-labelledby="room-h">
      <h2 id="room-h">The Practice Room</h2>
      <p>The Practice Room is where capacity planners work the open problems together. What we conclude is published here, credited by name.</p>
      <RoomStatus />
      <p>{settingUp() ? `Once it opens: ${rhythm.call.toLowerCase()}, with a newcomer half-hour first, and a kind answer to a first question within ${room.firstAnswerHours} hours.` : `${rhythm.call}, with a newcomer half-hour first. A first question gets a kind answer within ${room.firstAnswerHours} hours.`} The room is invitation-only, so it stays practitioner-only. Newcomers are invited too; say you’re new when you write.</p>
      <p><strong>How to ask.</strong> Write to <a href={mail('Join the Practice Room')}>{contact}</a> with your sector and one problem you care about. Your employer is optional. {inboxLine()}</p>
      <NextCall />
      <RoomRule />
      <p><a class="more" href="/community/">How the room works</a> · <a class="more" href="/circle/">The founding circle</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="prose reading" aria-labelledby="private-h">
      <h2 id="private-h">Private routes</h2>
      <p>Not everyone can comment in public, and that’s fine. Write to <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a>. We post for you, with credit if you want it. {inboxLine()}</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>A comment or a correction.</strong> Send the passage and what you’d change. It’s posted in the right thread, with or without your name.</li>
        <li><strong>A problem you can’t share yet.</strong> Ask for a private pre-check. A written reply comes within {room.precheckHours} hours. <a href="/sharing-safely/">How the pre-check works</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>A hand raised for a role.</strong> Say which <a href="/roles/">role</a> you’d like. It stays private: only whoever reads the inbox sees it.</li>
      </ul>
      {coOrganizers.length > 0
        ? <p class="muted">Co-organizers: {coOrganizers.map((p) => p.name).join(', ')}.</p>
        : <p class="muted">Co-organizers are being invited now. They’re named on <a href="/circle/">the circle page</a> once they agree.</p>}
    </section>

    <section class="newhere prose reading" id="new" aria-labelledby="new-h">
      <h2 id="new-h">New here? How commenting works</h2>
      <p><strong>What this is.</strong> The seed paper is a request for comments: a draft shared on purpose, so the people who do the work can improve it. The internet’s own standards have been written this way since 1969.</p>
      <p><strong>How to comment</strong></p>
      <ol>
        <li>Select any sentence in the paper or the guide. A <strong>Discuss this passage</strong> button appears at the bottom of the screen. Or use <strong>Discuss</strong> at the end of any page.</li>
        <li>GitHub opens. If you aren’t signed in, sign in or create a free account. It takes a minute, and you don’t need to know anything about code.</li>
        <li>The passage you picked is quoted for you. Add your comment and press <strong>Start discussion</strong>.</li>
      </ol>
      <p><strong>What happens next.</strong> The author reads every thread and replies. Others can join in. When a thread points to a change, it follows <a href="/how-it-grows/">How it grows</a>, and everyone who helped is credited by name.</p>
      <p><strong>A good comment can be one sentence.</strong> <span class="eg">“This doesn’t match what I’ve seen, because…” · “Here’s a public source for this: …” · “My team does this differently: …”</span></p>
      <p><strong>No GitHub account?</strong> Write to <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a>. Your comment gets posted for you, with credit if you want it.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="where-h">
      <h2 class="group-title reading" id="where-h">Where it happens</h2>
      <ul class="cards cards--3">
        <li><h3>On GitHub</h3><p>The public record. Each body-of-knowledge page ends with <strong>Discuss</strong> and <strong>Suggest an edit</strong>. Discussions hold questions, proposals, terms, cases and sources. Every decision is written down in its thread.</p><p><a class="more" href={`${c.repo}/discussions`}>Discussions</a> · <a class="more" href={c.repo}>Repository</a></p></li>
        <li><h3>In the Practice Room</h3><p>The closed room, for working out loud, being set up now. Topic channels, a monthly call and bring-your-problem reviews, under the room rules. What it concludes comes back to GitHub and this site.</p><p><a class="more" href="/community/">The Practice Room</a></p></li>
        <li><h3>On LinkedIn</h3><p>LinkedIn carries news only: new versions, open questions and call dates. The conversation happens on GitHub and in the Practice Room.</p><p>{c.linkedinPage && <a class="more" href={c.linkedinPage}>The page</a>}</p></li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="group-title reading" id="kinds-h">Ways to contribute</h2>
      <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-labelledby="kinds-h">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>You want to…</th><th>For example</th><th>Do this</th><th>Size</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>{kinds.map(([a, b, d, e]) => <tr><td><strong>{a}</strong></td><td>{b}</td><td set:html={d} /><td>{e}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="reading"><a href="/contributing/">Contributing, step by step</a>, from a two-minute comment to a pull request. New to the field? <a href="/start/">Start here</a> picks a door for you. Want something to try at work? <a href="/tools/">Tools for Monday</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="prose reading" aria-labelledby="share-h">
      <h2 id="share-h">Before you share</h2>
      <p>These keep the practice safe to contribute to, and safe to use. <a href="/sharing-safely/">Sharing safely</a> has the full ladder and ten checks.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Anything confidential to a current or former employer, client or vendor stays out.</li>
        <li>Names of internal systems, projects or teams that aren’t already public stay out.</li>
        <li>Real internal numbers stay out: ratios, costs, utilization, forecasts, lead times. Use shapes, indexes or bands, or invent illustrative numbers and label them.</li>
        <li>“I’ve seen the data, trust me” isn’t evidence. If it isn’t public, it’s labeled argued or unmeasured.</li>
        <li>Sales pitches stay out, including the steward’s.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>You contribute in a personal capacity. If you’re unsure what your employer allows, ask your own employer. This is not legal advice.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="prose reading" aria-labelledby="credit-h">
      <h2 id="credit-h">Credit, licence and conduct</h2>
      <p>Credit lands on <a href="/contributors/">Contributors</a> when your contribution is merged or used, not only at the next edition. Being listed doesn’t mean you endorse every word. It means you helped build it.</p>
      <p>By contributing text you license it under CC BY-SA 4.0, like the rest of the content; code is MIT. There’s nothing else to sign. Everyone follows the <a href="/code-of-conduct/">code of conduct</a>, and the <a href="/community/#room-rules">room rules</a> apply in the Practice Room.</p>
      <p>Want to help edit? Editors review edits, call rough consensus and assemble each edition. <a href="/governance/">How editors are chosen</a>, or see every open <a href="/roles/">role</a>.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
